
Problem 3: Secure Login & Access Level System
Problem Statement

A system checks:

Username and password match stored values.

Access level determined using bitwise flags:

1 → Read

2 → Write

4 → Execute

User has permission value = 5.
Question

Write a program to:

Validate login credentials.

Check which permissions user has.

Print access rights.

Code
stored_user = "admin"
stored_pass = "secure123"

username = "admin"
password = "secure123"

permissions = 5   # Binary 101

login_success = (username == stored_user) and (password == stored_pass)

print("Login Successful:", login_success)

if login_success:
    print("Permissions:")
    print("Read Access:", bool(permissions & 1))
    print("Write Access:", bool(permissions & 2))
    print("Execute Access:", bool(permissions & 4))
Output
Login Successful: True
Permissions:
Read Access: True
Write Access: False
Execute Access: True
Observation

Relational operators validate credentials.

Logical AND ensures both username & password match.

Bitwise AND extracts permission flags.

Binary representation helps manage access control efficiently.
